    # Wait, the i-th alien becomes adult at year i. So, for each year from 1 to N, when the i-th alien becomes adult, the adults are those who have index <= i (since they became adults at their respective years). So, for the i-th alien, when they become adult, the number of adults who have at least one stone is the number of aliens j where j <= i and A[j] >= 1. But since the i-th alien is also an adult, they will give a stone to the i-th alien if they have at least one stone.
